# The image builds its own dependency tree (`npm install`) and its own bundle
# (`npm run build`). The later `COPY apps/<app> apps/<app>` must never overlay
# the build context's copies on top of them: a host-side
# apps/<app>/node_modules/@firebase/app shadows the hoisted one, so
# initializeApp() and getAuth() read different component registries and the app
# dies at startup with "Component auth has not been registered yet" -- a blank
# white screen, with the bundle itself still serving 200.
# Note that .gitignore does NOT apply to a Docker build context -- only this file does.
node_modules
**/node_modules
**/dist

# Never ship local secrets or dev TLS keys into a build layer. The .cert
# exclusion is safe: those files are read only by vite.config.ts for the dev
# server's `server.https`, which `vite build` never evaluates.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/.cert

.git

# Native build inputs and outputs. apps/mobile now builds from the repo root
# (it needs packages/shared for the shared <Logo/>), which pulled its android/,
# .expo/ and any locally built .apk/.aab into the build context -- hundreds of
# MB shipped to the daemon on every build, none of it used by the web bundle.
# The web build only ever reads src/, app.config.js and package.json.
**/.expo
**/android
**/ios
**/*.apk
**/*.aab
**/*.keystore
**/*.jks
**/*.log
